    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d649">

                <pb facs="0756" n="658" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg658"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2945: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-09-07T12:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 7,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received September 7—6:50
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>243. Williams<anchor n="20" xml:id="d649-f1"/> advises he assumed office of
                    associate inspector general Wine, Tobacco September 1st. States that, pending
                    formal establishment [of] inspectorate general and to facilitate collection [of]
                    necessary data, he has been instructed as tentative measure to finance [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">function?</hi>] under orders [of] Premier and Minister
                    of Finance. Copies of all reports, accounts and returns necessary for full
                    investigation of the revenue concerned will be furnished by [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">to?</hi>] him.</p>
                <pb facs="0757" n="659" xml:id="pg659"/>
                <p>Legation has not received reply from the Chinese Government regarding extension
                    of option Pacific Development Corporation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d649-f1" n="20" xml:id="d649-f1-content">
                <p>Charles L. L. Williams, formerly of U.S. consular service.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
